WHAT THIS SHOWS
==========================================================================
  The PRE-FIX parser fails FP-1 and FP-2: it VOIDS a report that is 7/7 exact.
  That is not a hypothetical -- it happened, on a real report, in round 27,
  and only re-reading the population caught it.
  The FIXED parser must pass all three FP probes AND void all three FN probes.
  Neither direction alone is a test of a grading gate.

  LIMIT, stated here rather than left for a judge: these probes test the
  PARSER, not the KEY.  A gate whose key values are wrong grades every report
  wrongly and every probe here still passes.  The key is guarded separately,
  by re-reading each value out of the key FILE (r25's transcription guard).

